Website UI Redesign – TN CM Helpline Portal
Project Overview:
This project focuses on redesigning the user interface of the Tamil Nadu Chief Minister (CM) Helpline Portal to improve usability, accessibility, and overall user experience. The existing website was analyzed to identify issues such as cluttered layouts, inconsistent visual hierarchy, limited color contrast, and navigation challenges that could affect user interaction.
The redesign introduces a modern and user-friendly interface that enhances clarity, simplifies navigation, and improves information accessibility for citizens. The new design follows core UI/UX principles, including consistency, visual hierarchy, accessibility, responsive design, and intuitive user flows.
Objectives:
Improve the overall visual appearance of the portal.
Simplify navigation and information architecture.
Enhance readability through better typography and spacing.
Create a clear visual hierarchy for important services and announcements.
Problems Identified:
Crowded and outdated interface design.
Weak visual hierarchy and inconsistent spacing.
Difficult navigation for accessing key services.
Limited emphasis on important actions and information.
Inconsistent color usage affecting readability.
Design Improvements
Modernized homepage with a cleaner layout.
Improved navigation menu structure.
Consistent color palette aligned with government branding.
Better typography and spacing for enhanced readability.
Redesigned service cards and action buttons for easier interaction.
Mobile-friendly responsive design.
Clear call-to-action sections for grievance submission and status tracking.
Tools Used:
Figma (UI Design & Prototyping)
UI/UX Design Principles
Wireframing and User Flow Analysis
Outcome:
The redesigned TN CM Helpline Portal provides a more organized, accessible, and visually appealing experience, enabling citizens to access government services and grievance-related information more efficiently and effectively.
